[11.331193, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[11.3314, "o", "2. **Parse and Format Dates**: Convert the '\"'\"'last_login'\"'\"' ISO 8601 timestamp into a date string in the format '\"'\"'YYYY-MM-DD'\"'\"'.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[11.331495, "o", "3. **Extract and Rename Fields**:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[11.331526, "o", "   - Extract '\"'\"'id'\"'\"' as '\"'\"'user_id'\"'\"'.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[11.331562, "o", "   - Extract '\"'\"'username'\"'\"'.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[11.331593, "o", "   - Extract '\"'\"'email'\"'\"'.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[11.331613, "o", "> "]
[11.331663, "o", "   - Extract and format '\"'\"'last_login'\"'\"'.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[11.331685, "o", "> "]
[11.331744, "o", "   - Extract the count of roles as '\"'\"'role_count'\"'\"'.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[11.331763, "o", "> "]
[11.33192, "o", "   - Extract the first role from the '\"'\"'roles'\"'\"' array as '\"'\"'primary_role'\"'\"' (if roles exist, otherwise null).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[11.332055, "o", "4. **Sort Users**: Sort the resulting users alphabetically by their '\"'\"'username'\"'\"' in ascending order.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[11.332064, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[11.33222, "o", "5. **Output Format**: The output must be a JSON array of objects formatted with indentation of 2 spaces.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[11.332487, "o", "6. **Save Command**: Save the exact jq command you execute to a file named '\"'\"'/app/cmd.sh'\"'\"'. This file should contain the complete jq command used to generate the output, including all options and arguments.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[11.332535, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
