[11.333939, "o", "   4. The output will be redirected to '\"'\"'/app/active_users_report.json'\"'\"'\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[11.33399, "o", "   5. jq will be executed exactly once with all these components\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>    \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[11.334031, "o", "\u001b[?2004h>    Requirements for the YAML file:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[11.334044, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[11.334136, "o", "   - The '\"'\"'args'\"'\"' list should contain complete jq arguments, with both flags and their values (if any)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[11.334193, "o", "   - Each argument should be a separate string in the list\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[11.334209, "o", "> "]
[11.334286, "o", "   - For flag-only arguments, include just the flag (e.g., '\"'\"'--unbuffered'\"'\"', '\"'\"'--tab'\"'\"')\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[11.334307, "o", "> "]
[11.334403, "o", "   - For arguments with values, include both the flag and value as a single string (e.g., '\"'\"'--argjson min_count 5'\"'\"')\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[11.334491, "o", "   - Do not include the jq command itself, the filter expression, or file paths in the args list\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[11.334533, "o", "> "]
[11.334615, "o", "   - File paths other than the required input file '\"'\"'/app/users.json'\"'\"' and output redirections should not appear in the args\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[11.334693, "o", "   - The filter should be a single string containing the complete jq filter expression\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[11.334708, "o", "> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[11.334948, "o", "**Note on examples below**: In the following Data Schema sections, all content following the '\"'\"'#'\"'\"' symbol is just explanatory commentary and will NOT appear in the actual JSON files. These comments are only provided to clarify the structure and requirements.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[11.335019, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> **Input Data Schema**:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[11.335086, "o", "The input JSON file '\"'\"'/app/users.json'\"'\"' is an array of user objects with the following structure:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> [\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[11.3351, "o", "\u001b[?2004h>   {\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[11.335119, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[11.335178, "o", "    \"id\": 1,                  # Unique numeric identifier for the user\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[11.33526, "o", "    \"username\": \"john_doe\",   # User'\"'\"'s unique username (string)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[11.335305, "o", "    \"email\": \"john@example.com\",  # User'\"'\"'s email address (string)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[11.335314, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[11.335419, "o", "    \"status\": \"active\",       # User status: '\"'\"'active'\"'\"' or '\"'\"'inactive'\"'\"'\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[11.335488, "o", "    \"last_login\": \"2024-10-02T20:59:10.109812Z\",  # ISO 8601 timestamp (UTC) of the last login\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[11.335564, "o", "    \"roles\": [\"admin\", \"editor\"]  # Array of roles assigned to the user (may be empty)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[11.335609, "o", ">   },\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[11.335642, "o", "  ...\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ]\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[11.335671, "o", "**Output Data Schema**:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[11.335759, "o", "The output JSON file '\"'\"'/app/active_users_report.json'\"'\"' must be an array of objects with the following structure:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[11.335783, "o", "> [\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>   {\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[11.335804, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[11.335856, "o", "    \"user_id\": 1,                 # Derived from '\"'\"'id'\"'\"' in input \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[11.335875, "o", "> "]
[11.335926, "o", "    \"username\": \"john_doe\",       # Retained from input \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[11.335975, "o", "    \"email\": \"john@example.com\",  # Retained from input \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[11.335985, "o", "> "]
[11.336055, "o", "    \"last_login\": \"2024-10-02\",   # Formatted from '\"'\"'last_login'\"'\"' in input\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[11.336079, "o", "> "]
[11.336132, "o", "    \"role_count\": 2,              # Count of '\"'\"'roles'\"'\"' from input\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[11.336225, "o", "    \"primary_role\": \"admin\"       # If '\"'\"'roles'\"'\"' is empty, this must be null (JSON null, not \"null\")\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[11.336255, "o", "\u001b[?2004h>   },\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[11.33628, "o", "  ...\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ]\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[11.336304, "o", "> **Requirements**:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[11.336326, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[11.336424, "o", "- You must use jq to perform this transformation. Using other programming languages (e.g., Python, Ruby) is strictly prohibited.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[11.336453, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[11.336505, "o", "- Ensure that the output JSON is properly formatted with 2-space indentation.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[11.33659, "o", "- The output file must be created at the exact path '\"'\"'/app/active_users_report.json'\"'\"'.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[11.336612, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[11.336755, "o", "- The jq command used to generate the output(along with the output redirection) must be saved to '\"'\"'/app/cmd.sh'\"'\"'. This file will be used to verify the correctness of your solution.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[11.336781, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[11.33689, "o", "- The jq arguments and filter must be saved to '\"'\"'/app/jq_args.yaml'\"'\"' as specified in the instructions above.  '; tmux wait -S done\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
